    5813	## §G. The Multiplicative Regime — Beyond the W-Trick Wall
    5814	
    5815	**Why this section exists:** S87 (Gowers `U^k` of χ_P), S88 (Anderson
    5816	Lyapunov of χ_P-Schrödinger), and S89 (parity-calibrated depth-2
    5817	threshold circuits) jointly established a triple confirmation that
    5818	**every detectable deviation of χ_P from random is exactly the Hardy-
    5819	Littlewood singular series mod q, fully removed by the Green-Tao
    5820	W-trick**. The additive / spectral / circuit-complexity regime on the
    5821	*bare prime indicator* is now a closed family. Future productive
    5822	attacks must move to the **multiplicative regime**: Liouville `λ(n)`,
    5823	Möbius `μ(n)`, von Mangoldt `Λ(n)` truncated, etc. These are predicted
    5824	to be Gowers-uniform *without* W-tricking (Green-Tao 2012 Möbius/
    5825	nilsequence orthogonality theorem). Any deviation found here is fresh
    5826	territory the W-trick framework cannot explain.
    5827	
    5828	The next-action recommendation from S88 explicitly flagged this pivot.
    5829	This section is its concrete realisation.
