    370	multi-affine polynomial `f_χ_P^{(n)}(x_1, ..., x_n) = Σ_{S ⊆ [n], \mathrm{val}(S) \in \mathrm{PRIMES}} ∏_{i \in S} x_i`
    371	where `\mathrm{val}(S) := Σ_{i \in S} 2^{i-1}`. The Mulmuley-Sohoni 2001
    372	GCT program seeks formula / determinant lower bounds on a polynomial
    373	`f` via *orbit closure containment* in `\mathrm{End}(V) \cdot f` and
    374	*occurrence obstructions* — irreducible `GL(V)`-representations
    375	appearing in the coordinate ring `\mathbb{C}[\overline{GL_n \cdot f}]`
    376	but NOT in the determinant orbit closure. Question: identify a
    377	representation-theoretic GCT obstruction proving `f_χ_P^{(n)}` has
    378	formula size super-polynomial in `n` (equivalently, χ_P ∉ NC^1
    379	unconditionally), OR identify a GCT-style obstruction to TC^0
    380	computability that does not reduce to AKS-family closures (E5.3,
    381	E7.10) or to Brandt-style diagonalisation (E5.8).
